cJSONUtils_MergePatch: heap use-after-free when the target is not an object and the patch lies inside it -- the variant of issue #1060 (CVE-2026-87933) that PR #1065 left open.

From cJSON PR #1109, https://github.com/DaveGamble/cJSON/pull/1109 (head 97e09fcb2129b27c768fc86d5a1b4282ca6d716e),
open and unmerged on 2026-11-17; its tests/ hunks left out. Applied by build/vendorfetch.sh
to cJSON master 6d9f2443ab071f86e5d9b43025a40929ec41c46c, after the patches numbered before it.
Drop it once a cJSON release carries the fix.

diff --git a/cJSON_Utils.c b/cJSON_Utils.c
index 4f3a9ed..02040e9 100644
--- a/cJSON_Utils.c
+++ b/cJSON_Utils.c
@@ -1335,8 +1335,20 @@ static cJSON *merge_patch(cJSON *target, const cJSON * const patch, const cJSON_
 
     if (!cJSON_IsObject(target))
     {
+        /* The patch may be part of target: deleting target would free it.
+         * Work from a copy, as for non-object patches above. */
+        cJSON *patch_copy = cJSON_Duplicate(patch, 1);
+        cJSON *result = cJSON_CreateObject();
+        if ((patch_copy == NULL) || (result == NULL))
+        {
+            cJSON_Delete(patch_copy);
+            cJSON_Delete(result);
+            return NULL;
+        }
         cJSON_Delete(target);
-        target = cJSON_CreateObject();
+        result = merge_patch(result, patch_copy, case_sensitive);
+        cJSON_Delete(patch_copy);
+        return result;
     }
 
     patch_child = patch->child;
